#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:5
msgid "AD7768 driver"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:7
msgid ""
"ADC driver for Analog Devices Inc. AD7768 and AD7768-4 devices. The module "
"name is ``ad7768``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:11
msgid "Supported devices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:13
msgid "The following chips are supported by this driver:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:15
msgid ""
"`AD7768 <https://www.analog.com/en/products/ad7768.html>`_ - 8-channel, 24-"
"bit simultaneous sampling ADC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:17
msgid ""
"`AD7768-4 <https://www.analog.com/en/products/ad7768-4.html>`_ - 4-channel, "
"24-bit simultaneous sampling ADC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:21
msgid "Supported features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:24
msgid "Clock sources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:26
msgid ""
"The master clock source is selected using the ``clock-names`` device tree "
"property:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:29
msgid ""
"``mclk`` selects a CMOS clock on XTAL2/MCLK. CLK_SEL must be low and XTAL1 "
"must be connected to DGND."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:31
msgid ""
"``xtal`` selects a crystal connected between XTAL1 and XTAL2. CLK_SEL must "
"be high. The driver drives FILTER/GPIO4 high and keeps channel 4 on the "
"AD7768 or channel 2 on the AD7768-4 enabled to maintain crystal excitation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:34
msgid ""
"``lvds`` selects a differential clock on XTAL1 and XTAL2. CLK_SEL must be "
"high. The driver drives FILTER/GPIO4 low before enabling the LVDS input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:37
msgid "GPIO4 is reserved when ``xtal`` or ``lvds`` is selected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:40
msgid "Power modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:42
msgid "The AD7768 family supports three power and performance modes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:44
msgid "**Low power mode** - Optimized for lowest power consumption"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:45
msgid "**Median mode** - Balanced power and performance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:46
msgid "**Fast mode** - Highest performance with maximum sampling rates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:48
msgid ""
"The driver initializes the device in fast mode and uses the maximum fast-"
"mode output data rate as the default sampling frequency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:51
msgid ""
"When buffered capture starts, the driver selects the lowest-noise mode that "
"can produce the requested output data rates for all enabled channels. Where "
"output data rates overlap, fast mode is preferred over median mode, and "
"median mode is preferred over low power mode. This prioritizes the lower RMS "
"noise and higher dynamic range offered by a faster mode at the same output "
"data rate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:58
msgid "Data output configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:60
msgid "The devices support flexible serial data output configurations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:63
msgid "AD7768 data lines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:65 ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:72
msgid "1 data line (DOUT0) - Standard single-lane output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:66
msgid "2 data lines (DOUT0, DOUT1) - Dual-lane output for higher throughput"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:67
msgid "8 data lines (DOUT0-DOUT7) - Maximum throughput, one line per channel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:70
msgid "AD7768-4 data lines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:73
msgid "4 data lines (DOUT0-DOUT3) - Maximum throughput, one line per channel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:75
msgid ""
"The number of data lines can be configured via the ``adi,data-lines-number`` "
"device tree property. If omitted, the driver uses the maximum supported by "
"the selected variant: eight lines for AD7768 and four lines for AD7768-4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:80
msgid "Channel configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:82
msgid "Each channel can be individually configured with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:85
msgid "Channel modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:87
msgid "**Mode A** - First set of filter and decimation settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:88
msgid "**Mode B** - Second set of filter and decimation settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:90
msgid ""
"The hardware provides two mode profiles (A and B), each holding one "
"(frequency, filter) combination. When buffered capture is started, enabled "
"channels are grouped by their configured (frequency, filter) pair. Up to two "
"distinct groups are supported; the driver automatically assigns each group "
"to a mode slot and programs the hardware accordingly. If the enabled "
"channels request more than two distinct pairs, buffer setup fails and "
"capture does not start."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:99
msgid "Precharge and reference buffers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:101
msgid "Per-channel buffer control for optimal signal integrity:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:103
msgid "Positive input precharge buffer (``adi,prechargebuf-pos-enable``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:104
msgid "Negative input precharge buffer (``adi,prechargebuf-neg-enable``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:105
msgid "Positive reference buffer (``adi,refbuf-pos-enable``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:106
msgid "Negative reference buffer (``adi,refbuf-neg-enable``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:109
msgid "Common mode voltage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:111
msgid ""
"The VCM pin provides a buffered common-mode voltage output used to bias the "
"analog inputs. The driver exposes this as a standard voltage regulator "
"provider under a ``regulators`` subnode in the device tree. Supported output "
"voltage levels are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:116
msgid ""
"(AVDD1 - AVSS) / 2 - Mid-supply (hardware default), reported as half the "
"voltage provided by ``avdd1-supply``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:118
msgid "1,650,000 µV - 1.65V"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:119
msgid "2,500,000 µV - 2.5V"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:120
msgid "2,140,000 µV - 2.14V"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:122
msgid ""
"The regulator can be enabled and disabled at runtime using the standard "
"regulator framework interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:125
msgid ""
"The VCM circuitry is associated with channel 0. When VCM is used externally, "
"``channel@0`` must be present in the device tree and channel 0 must remain "
"enabled in the active scan mask. Placing channel 0 in standby disables the "
"VCM output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:131
msgid "Filter types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:133
msgid "Two digital filter types are available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:135
msgid "**Wideband** - Optimized for wide bandwidth applications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:136
msgid ""
"**Sinc5** - Fifth-order sinc filter for high rejection of out-of-band noise"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:139
msgid "IIO backend support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:141
msgid ""
"The driver integrates with IIO backends (e.g., AXI ADC) for high-speed data "
"capture and DMA operations. Features include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:144
msgid "Automatic channel enable/disable based on scan mask"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:145
msgid "CRC on data interface. CRC replaces the header every 4th output sample."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:146
msgid "High-throughput buffered data acquisition"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:149
msgid "GPIO controller"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:151
msgid ""
"The AD7768 includes a 5-pin GPIO controller for auxiliary digital I/O "
"operations. The GPIO pins can be configured as inputs or outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:154
msgid ""
"GPIO4 is reserved when a crystal or LVDS master clock is used. GPIO0 through "
"GPIO3 remain available in these configurations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:158
msgid "Device attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:160
msgid "The following IIO attributes are available for each enabled channel:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:163
msgid "Voltage scale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:169 ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:183
#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:201 ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:216
msgid "Attribute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:170 ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:184
#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:202 ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:217
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:171
msgid "``in_voltage<N>_scale``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:172
msgid ""
"Scale in millivolts per least significant bit for signed 24-bit data, "
"calculated as twice the differential reference voltage used by channel N "
"divided by 2\\ :sup:`24`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:177
msgid "Sampling frequency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:185
msgid "``in_voltage<N>_sampling_frequency``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:186
msgid ""
"Requested sampling frequency in Hz for channel N. Enabled channels are "
"grouped into up to two profiles at capture time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:188
msgid "``in_voltage<N>_sampling_frequency_available``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:189
msgid ""
"Available sampling frequencies in Hz for channel N across all power modes, "
"based on the master clock frequency. Buffer setup fails if no single power "
"mode supports the frequencies requested by all enabled channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:195
msgid "Filter configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:203
msgid "``in_voltage<N>_filter_type``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:204
msgid ""
"Requested filter type for channel N: \"wideband\" or \"sinc5\". It is "
"grouped with sampling frequency at capture time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:206
msgid "``in_voltage<N>_filter_type_available``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:207
msgid "Available filter types for channel N: \"wideband sinc5\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:210
msgid "Per-channel calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:218
msgid "``in_voltage<N>_calibbias``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:219
msgid "Signed 24-bit two's complement channel offset register value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:220
msgid "``in_voltage<N>_calibscale``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:221
msgid "Raw unsigned 24-bit channel gain register value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:222
msgid "``in_voltage<N>_convdelay``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:223
msgid ""
"Per-channel conversion delay. The driver exposes the sync phase offset value "
"in seconds with picosecond precision. Resolution and valid range depend on "
"the decimation ratio in use (see datasheet Table 32)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad7768.rst:229
msgid "Device buffers"
msgstr ""

